\node at (1.7,-0.35) {$\text{(i)}$};
\fill[gray!35] (4.2,0) rectangle (7.6,2.5);
\fill[white] (5.43,1.1) circle (0.8);
\fill[white] (6.37,1.1) circle (0.8);
\draw (4.2,0) rectangle (7.6,2.5);
\draw (5.43,1.1) circle (0.8);
\draw (6.37,1.1) circle (0.8);
\node at (4.92,2.15) {$A$};
\node at (6.88,2.15) {$B$};
\node at (5.9,-0.35) {$\text{(ii)}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The same region is shaded on both diagrams, so $(A \cup B)' = A' \cap B'$.

